      "body": "Bare `except:` swallows `KeyboardInterrupt` and `SystemExit`, making it impossible to interrupt with Ctrl+C. PEP 8 explicitly recommends against bare `except:` for this reason.\n\nChanged `except:` to `except Exception:` in 11 parsing/serialization fallback paths (5 files):\n- `function_call/step3_detector.py` (2 sites)\n- `function_call/llama32_detector.py` (3 sites)\n- `observability/trace.py` (1 site)\n- `entrypoints/openai/encoding_dsv32.py` (1 site)\n- `utils/rpd_utils.py` (4 sites: skip-on-missing fallbacks for optional rocpd tables)\n\nThe `encoding_dsv4.py` / `encoding_dsv41.py` hunks from the original revision were dropped on rebase — #45315 removed those modules upstream.\n\nImport-fallback and feature-probe bare `except:` sites (`protocol.py`, `minicpmo.py`, `common.py`, kernel import probes) are intentionally left alone — they need to catch any exception from a broken install or a capability probe.\n\nAfter this, no unintentional bare `except:` remains in `python/sglang/srt`. No behavior change on existing inputs. `KeyboardInterrupt` and `SystemExit` now propagate instead of being swallowed.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #40257261981](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40257261981)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #40257262212](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40257262212)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #40257261977](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40257261977)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
